.listen_command` (Bryan's chezmoi config sets [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]`sase-listen render {target} -e full -o {audio}`) with its output [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]streamed unchanged, and binds the published episode as the PDF's [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]companion audio. `bob highlights scan` then writes a ref note with [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]an audio player. When the target is already captured, `--listen` [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]attaches the new episode to the existing ref note instead. Every [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]article or paper Bryan listens to ends up tracked in his Obsidian [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]ref system. Nothing is ever written to the vault unless every step [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]succeeded.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]6[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]5[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202610/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]highlights_create_listen.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202610/highlights_create_listen.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]bob-cli-4s[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/bobs-org/bob-cli--beads/blob/main/pages/bob-cli-4s/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Configurable listen command contract and runner[/bold #D7AFFF]               [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]listen-command[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]listen-command: add highlights.listen_command plus its env override, a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]template parser with shell-quoted {target}/{pdf}/{audio}/{title} [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]placeholders, a runner that streams output unchanged and verifies the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]MP3 written to {audio}, and a doctor row.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]URL fetcher, arXiv identity and metadata, and shared dedupe[/bold #D7AFFF]   [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]fetch-arxiv[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]fetch-arxiv: add a curl-based fetcher that validates every redirect hop,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]arXiv URL parsing that mirrors sase-listen, arXiv API metadata, the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]short-title stem rule, and a shared dedupe module with arXiv and legacy [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]url keys.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]create accepts local PDFs, PDF URLs, and arXiv papers[/bold #D7AFFF]         [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]pdf-targets[dim] · [dim][/dim]after fetch-arxiv[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]pdf-targets: add TARGET classification to create, a stamp-as-is PDF [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]route with title, stem, and validation rules, private scratch staging, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the new -N/-T flags and per-kind ref-type defaults, explicit --audio on [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]every route, CLI tests with a fake curl, and docs/highlights-create.md.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]create routes web article URLs through the clip engine[/bold #D7AFFF]        [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]article-targets[dim] · [dim][/dim]after pdf-targets[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]article-targets: refactor clip into a callable engine and route create's[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]HTML and bot-walled URL targets through it with create's options, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]explicit companion audio support, and tests.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Wire --listen into create and clip, with attach mode[/bold #D7AFFF]          [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]create-listen[dim] · [dim][/dim]after listen-command, article-targets[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]create-listen: add -L/--listen to create and clip on every route with [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]all-or-nothing ordering, attach mode for already-captured targets, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]dry-run and reports, fake-listen CLI tests, docs, and the chezmoi [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]listen_command line.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Live end-to-end verification on athena[/bold #D7AFFF]                        [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]live-verify[dim] · [dim][/dim]after create-listen[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]live-verify: build bob and exercise every target kind into a scratch [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]vault, run one real unpublished sase-listen render under a TTY, scan the[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]scratch vault to prove the ref note gets the player, fix what breaks, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and record follow-ups.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"bob-cli-4s","llm_provider":"muse","model":"muse-spark-1.3-contributor","patch_name":"gh_bobs-org__bob-cli","phase_bead_id":"bob-cli-4s.1","reasoning_effort":"high","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-6974eebbac20407db79fa4a41c6ca23b","started_at":"2026-10-06T19:47:44.472744+00:00","state":"completed"},{"capabilities":{"durably_revivable":true,"historically_viewable":true,"missing_requirements":[],"restartable":true},"commits":[{"committed_at":1791317203,"sha":"fb77b56e3b6b20776787ab809631a7a64a777be2","subject":"feat(highlights): add native highlights_ref fetch, arxiv, clip, and dedupe"}],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"chat":{"digest":"e06b70b7b356f7cda628b8ec550e32032a8964e0e604e41eedb8b18e4b00c07b","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-4s.2/chat.md","size_bytes":4271},"commits":{"digest":"870f2ed2a7475fb68f1d9eb8ac9377e4b7def84117c1c8b79e232e1f346b2e70","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-4s.2/commits.json","size_bytes":252},"embed